 ### Parameters
-*   **MaxTriangle:** The maximum number of triangles allowed in the output mesh. Used to prevent buffer overflow. Typical values depend on the scene complexity and available GPU memory [S1].
-*   **Scale:** A scalar factor used to transform grid coordinates to object space. Determines the physical size of the output mesh [S1].
-*   **Isovalue:** The threshold value for isosurface extraction. Vertices with values below this are considered inside [S1].
-*   **Chunk Size:** (Optional) The number of points processed in each iteration of the implicit function evaluation loop to limit GPU memory usage. Default value in some implementations: 262144 [S2].
-*   **One Over Size:** (Optional) Calculated as $1.0 / (size - 1)$. Used to normalize coordinates to the $[0, 1]$ range in caching variants [S3].
