+*   **One Over Size:** (Optional) Calculated as $1.0 / (size - 1)$. Used to normalize coordinates to the $[0, 1]$ range in caching variants [S4, unofficial].
 
 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Empty Cube:** If the selector is 0 (all vertices below isovalue) or 0xFF (all vertices above isovalue), the cube does not intersect the isosurface. The algorithm must return immediately to skip processing [S1].
-*   **Buffer Overflow:** If the number of generated triangles exceeds `MaxTriangle`, the atomic counter check prevents writing out of bounds. However, this results in an incomplete mesh. A cleanup pass is recommended to zero out unused buffer space [S1].
-*   **Gradient Calculation at Boundaries:** When calculating gradients using central differences, indices must be clamped to the grid boundaries to avoid out-of-bounds memory access [S1].
-*   **Precision:** Floating-point precision in interpolation and gradient calculation can affect surface smoothness. Using `float` (32-bit) is standard, but `double` may be needed for high-precision SDFs [S1].
