 ## Background
-Primal Grid Marching Cubes is a GPU adaptation of the classic Marching Cubes algorithm, originally described by Lorensen and Cline [S1]. The specific implementation referenced here is from the Unity sample project "ComputeMarchingCubes" by Keijiro [S1]. It leverages the Unity Compute Shader API and the new Mesh API to perform isosurface reconstruction directly on the GPU, avoiding CPU-GPU data transfer bottlenecks [S1]. The method is widely used in real-time volume rendering and implicit surface visualization within game engines and scientific visualization tools [S1].
